  "theoryOfChange": "Pure Hands describes a 'people-centered and results-driven approach' to achieve 'large-scale, measurable impact'. Their interventions are 'informed by context analysis, needs assessments, and continuous monitoring', and they 'adapt programs based on evolving needs, risks, and feedback, ensuring relevance and effectiveness'. They also detail their 'DATA SOURCES & METHODOLOGY', which includes a 'Primary Data Source, Pure Hands Cumulative Report (2013-2025)' and a 'Contextual Framework, Yemen Humanitarian Needs and Response Plan (HNRP) 2025'. Their 'Content Approach' outlines 'The Issue', 'Our Approach' (aligned with HNRP cluster objectives and response strategies), and 'Our Impact' (based on Pure Hands actual achievements and data). They also outline three programmatic pillars: immediate crisis response, sustainable development & climate resilience, and social cohesion program & peace & human development, all guided by humanitarian principles and a commitment to accountability, protection, gender equality, disability inclusion, and conflict sensitivity.",
